{{!-- /the-faith-received/dictionary/ — the Dictionnaire de Théologie
     Catholique, ported whole from the corpus site (its /dtc).

     THE CORPUS SITE'S DICTIONARY INSIDE THIS SITE: the search band (a
     headword in English or French, the count, the alphabet), the list
     of articles on the left, the article on the right with French and
     English paired paragraph by paragraph, the lane switch, the
     contents popover, previous/next, the reading-size control — driven
     by dtc.in02.js, the page's own engine. Extends `default`; the page's
     own top bar stays under our masthead. The 1,916 articles and the
     index are read from R2 through the library worker at v1/dictionary/
     — a copy of v1/dtc/, which that worker refuses by design (its
     reading of those files as raw French; see tfr-library/worker.js) and
     which the mo-tfr worker serves without CORS for this origin.

     Owner 2026-09-19: "fix this … just the aesthetics" — the page is the
     corpus site's page. The previous dictionary (faith-dictionary.js and
     the _dictionary partial, translate-on-open through the library
     worker) is unmounted, not deleted. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-port-surface-boot.js"}}&amp;frv=c6ea6e388eea3f2a" data-body-class="dtc-page"></script>
<div class="faith-port-dtc-page">
<header class="top">
  <span class="wm">Dictionary of Catholic Theology</span>
  <span class="sub">Vacant · Mangenot · Amann · Paris, 1899–1950</span>
  {{!-- The "← The Faith Received" link was removed (Ian, 2026-09-23:
       "Not necessary"); the TFR rail above already goes home.
       The search band sits inside the title bar, one line on a wide
       screen (Ian, 2026-09-23: "shrink the search bar width way down and
       then just combine these lines"). The engine finds #q, #count and
       #alpha by id, so where they sit does not matter to it. --}}
  <div class="sband">
    <input id="q" placeholder="Search headwords…" aria-label="Search the dictionary, headword or phrase" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" autofocus>
    <span class="count" id="count"></span>
    <nav class="alpha" id="alpha" aria-label="Alphabet"></nav>
  </div>
</header>
{{!-- Where you left off. Filled by the engine from the same position
     store the reader uses (corpus "dtc"); hidden while an article is
     open, because then you are already in one. --}}
<div class="dtc-resume" id="resume" hidden></div>
{{!-- Fold the index and the top bar (Ian, 2026-09-23). Outside #art,
     which the engine rewrites. faith-dtc-chrome.js. --}}
<div class="dtc-chrome">
  <button type="button" class="dtc-fold" data-dtc-fold="list" aria-controls="list" aria-expanded="true">Hide index</button>
  <button type="button" class="dtc-fold" data-dtc-expand aria-controls="list" aria-pressed="false">Expand index</button>
  <button type="button" class="dtc-fold" data-dtc-fold="top" aria-expanded="true">Hide search bar</button>
</div>
<template id="dtc-welcome"><div class="artscroll"><div class="inner">{{> "faith-received/_dtc-welcome"}}</div></div></template>
<div class="main">
  <div class="list" id="list" role="listbox" aria-label="Articles"></div>
  <div class="art" id="art"><div class="artscroll"><div class="inner">
    {{!-- 2026-09-22, Ian: the intro broke into one line per inline run
         (`.welcome` is also the subscriber /welcome/ page's class, and
         screen.css makes that a flex column), it was set in italics
         throughout, and it said too little about the work. Fuller copy,
         upright, in paragraphs. The unbreaking is in
         faith-port-surfaces.css. --}}
    {{> "faith-received/_dtc-welcome"}}
  </div></div></div>
</div>
